# Old GoDaddy WordPress site used /privacy-policy-2/ and /terms-and-conditions/
# slugs. After Netlify migration, canonical paths became /privacy and /terms.
# These 301s catch any in-the-wild references (old marketing materials,
# archived TCR submissions, search engine indexes, customer-saved bookmarks)
# so they don't hit 404 and break consent-flow verification.

